N:eli5
D:Explain a topic, codebase, document, concept, or error at a named audience's knowledge level and decision context. Calibrate vocabulary depth framing analogy and tone while preserving truth caveats and dignity. Route evidence audits to audit-verify-explain-grade-5 and tutorials or runbooks to technical-writing.
G:eli5 explain plain-language audience teaching communication analogy simplify manager child parent partner grade

U[8]:
  Explain a complex concept like the audience is five or at another named age
  Adapt code error or document explanations for a student manager engineer designer or executive
  Explain a topic to a parent partner child friend or colleague without condescension
  Break down jargon into a useful mental model and define essential terms
  Change depth vocabulary framing and examples without changing source facts
  Preserve uncertainty and safety boundaries in plain language
  Route audit verification and measured claims to audit-verify-explain-grade-5
  Route tutorials FAQs onboarding guides and runbooks to technical-writing

S[7]{n,step,details}:
  1,Identify audience and purpose,record age grade education role relationship prior knowledge decision and desired depth
  2,Understand the source,read relevant code documents errors or claims; do not translate an invented mechanism
  3,Choose the frame,lead with child student technical business design executive or relationship context without stereotyping
  4,Build four layers,start with what then one analogy then needed mechanism then why it matters to that audience
  5,Guard the analogy,map objects actions and outcomes; state its limit when a mismatch could create a wrong decision
  6,Calibrate language,define essential terms remove decorative jargon preserve caveats and never use childish tone as a synonym for simple
  7,Run the audience check,verify fit truth source attribution analogy depth so-what and route-out boundaries

R[13]:
  Explicit ELI5 without another audience defaults to age-five style
  Generic explain without an audience does not automatically become childlike
  Age role and relationship are calibration hypotheses not proof of knowledge
  Purpose comes before syntax or implementation detail
  One accurate analogy is better than several catchy metaphors
  Analogy is not evidence and must not reverse cause and effect
  Simple language keeps material caveats uncertainty numbers and attribution
  Technical audiences get proper terminology trade-offs and edge cases
  Managers and executives get impact risk options and decisions without invented ROI
  Never talk down to children adults family members or nontechnical roles
  Audit or verification requests route to audit-verify-explain-grade-5
  Tutorials runbooks FAQs and help-center content route to technical-writing
  Safety-critical explanation does not replace qualified medical legal financial or security ownership

E[6]{type,command}:
  Validate eval contract,node .agent-skills/eli5/scripts/validate-evals.mjs
  Default audience,ELI5 what a database index is
  Manager audience,Explain API rate limiting to my manager
  Technical audience,Explain eventual consistency to a senior backend engineer
  Audit route-out,Audit this performance fix and explain the verified result to a fifth grader
  Documentation route-out,Turn this explanation into an onboarding tutorial with steps
